    title: "Turkey police raid opposition TV station, halting live broadcasts",
    summary: "Halk TV says its staff are unable to enter the building in Istanbul, and a new manager was appointed to run the channel.",
    preview: "Turkish police have raided the headquarters of a pro-opposition TV channel, halting its live broadcasts. Halk TV said its employees were unable to enter the building in Istanbul on Wednesday morning, and that a new manager had been appointed to run the channel. Reports in Turkish media said financial crimes police were searching the building and 17 arrest warrants had been issued in the raid linked to the channel's owner. Halk TV has been seen by many in the country as being close to the opposition Republican People's Party (CHP).",
    body: "Turkish police have raided the headquarters of a pro-opposition TV channel, halting its live broadcasts.\n\nHalk TV said its employees were unable to enter the building in Istanbul on Wednesday morning, and that a new manager had been appointed to run the channel.\n\nReports in Turkish media said financial crimes police were searching the building and 17 arrest warrants had been issued in the raid linked to the channel's owner.\n\nHalk TV has been seen by many in the country as being close to the opposition Republican People's Party (CHP). It often voices criticism of President Recep Tayyip ErdoÄan's ruling AK party.\n\nIn May, a Turkish court removed the CHP leadership from running the party, in the legal move that the opposition said further cemented ErdoÄan's grip on power.\n\nMeanwhile, Istanbul's popular Mayor Ekrem ImamoÄlu, widely seen as ErdoÄan's biggest political rival, has been in prison for over a year over corruption accusations. He denies all the charges.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Published11 November 2025",
